  "summary": "Telia Rumal is a method for the oil treatment of yarn.",
  "description": "Telia Rumal is a method for the oil treatment of yarn. It originated from Chirala in Andhra Pradesh. At Chirala, in the Bapatla district of Andhra Pradesh where the craft started, the weavers had virtually stopped making Telia Rumals. People who acquired skill in this dying art took the lead to introduce this in Puttapaka village of Yadadri district in Telangana. Recently Puttapaka Telia Rumal was accorded with Geographical indication (GI) tag.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Telangana; registration 2020–21), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
